---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
---

<Base
  title="Privacy Policy | Andorra Private"
  description="Privacy Policy of Andorra Private under Andorran Llei 29/2021 (LQPD), including the concierge forms and the newsletter."
  path="/privacy"
>
  <div class="privacy-page">
    <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
    <p class="updated">Last updated: 11 October 2026</p>

    <p>
      This page explains how Andorra Private (“we”, “us” or “our”)
      collects, uses and protects your personal data when you visit
      privateandorra.com or send something through a form.
    </p>
    <p>
      A Spanish text of this policy is on
      <a href="/es/privacy">the Spanish page</a>.
    </p>

    <p>
      We process personal data in accordance with the
      <strong
        >Llei 29/2021, del 28 d’octubre, qualificada de protecció de dades
        personals</strong
      >
      of the Principality of Andorra (LQPD) and related regulations.
    </p>

    <h2>1. Data Controller</h2>
    <p>The data controller is the operator of privateandorra.com.</p>
    <p>
      For any privacy-related enquiry, write to:<br />
      <a href="mailto:hello@privateandorra.com">hello@privateandorra.com</a>
    </p>
    <p>
      There is no telephone number on this site. Privacy requests are
      handled in that inbox, in writing.
    </p>

    <h2>2. What data we collect</h2>
    <p>We may collect the following personal data:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Email address, and a name if you give one</li>
      <li>
        What you asked for (a reading pack, a plan, a partner introduction,
        or the newsletter), the route and timing you selected, a household
        count, and the message you wrote
      </li>
      <li>
        The plan text generated on the planner, if you ask for it to be
        emailed
      </li>
      <li>
        Whether you agreed that a summary may be sent to an independent
        licensed professional
      </li>
      <li>
        Technical data such as IP address, browser type and basic usage
        data, collected for security
      </li>
    </ul>
    <p>We do not ask for a telephone number.</p>

    <h2>3. Purpose and legal basis</h2>
    <p>We process your data for the following purposes:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>Sending what you asked for</strong> — the reading pack, a
        copy of the plan, or a reply to your message — based on your
        consent (Art. 6.1.a LQPD)
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>The newsletter</strong> — only if you subscribe, until you
        unsubscribe — based on your consent (Art. 6.1.a LQPD)
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>A partner introduction</strong> — only if you tick that
        box — based on your consent (Art. 6.1.a LQPD)
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Keeping the site secure</strong> — based on our legitimate
        interest (Art. 6.1.f LQPD)
      </li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      The plan is a text assembled in your browser from your answers and
      from figures cited on the page. It is not a decision on a residence
      file and it has no legal effect by itself.
    </p>

    <h2>4. Who we share data with</h2>
    <p>
      We use the following service providers, who may process data on our
      behalf:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>Neon</strong> — Postgres database for concierge and
        newsletter submissions, when a database connection is configured
      </li>
      <li><strong>Vercel</strong> — website hosting</li>
      <li>
        <strong>Formspree</strong> — the older email-only forms on other
        pages of this site
      </li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      These providers act as data processors. They may host data outside
      Andorra. We do not sell your personal data.
    </p>
    <p>
      If you tick the partner box, a summary (name, email, the letter the
      planner suggested, the timing you gave, and the message you wrote)
      may be emailed to an independent licensed professional: a lawyer,
      gestor, estate agent, insurer or school. They are not our processor
      for that message. They receive it so they can write to you. If you
      leave the box unticked, we do not send that summary.
    </p>
    <p>
      No card payment runs on this site today. If a payment is offered
      later, this policy will name the processor before a card is taken.
    </p>

    <h2>5. Data retention</h2>
    <p>
      We keep a request for as long as it takes to send what you asked
      for, and afterwards until you ask us to delete it. Newsletter
      addresses are kept until you unsubscribe. Technical logs are kept
      for a limited period for security.
    </p>

    <h2>6. Your rights</h2>
    <p>Under Andorran law (LQPD) you have the right to:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Access your personal data</li>
      <li>Rectify inaccurate data</li>
      <li>Request erasure of your data</li>
      <li>Restrict or object to processing</li>
      <li>Data portability (where applicable)</li>
      <li>Withdraw consent at any time</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      To exercise any of these rights, email
      <a href="mailto:hello@privateandorra.com">hello@privateandorra.com</a>.
      Withdrawing consent does not affect processing that took place
      before the withdrawal.
    </p>

    <h2>7. Complaints</h2>
    <p>
      If you believe your data protection rights have been infringed, you
      may lodge a complaint with the
      <strong>Agència Andorrana de Protecció de Dades (APDA)</strong>:
    </p>
    <p>
      C/ Dr. Vilanova, 15-17<br />
      AD500 Andorra la Vella<br />
      Principality of Andorra<br />
      <a href="https://www.apda.ad" target="_blank" rel="noopener">www.apda.ad</a>
    </p>

    <h2>8. Changes to this policy</h2>
    <p>
      We may update this Privacy Policy from time to time. The latest
      version will always be published on this page, with the date above.
    </p>
  </div>
</Base>
